\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li806\ri7634\sl244\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 2.2\expnd-1\expndtw-4  \expnd0\expndtw0 where\expnd-1\expndtw-4  \expnd0\expndtw0 you\expnd-1\expndtw-4  \expnd0\expndtw0 are\expnd-1\expndtw-4  \expnd0\expndtw0 presented\expnd-1\expndtw-4  \expnd0\expndtw0 with\expnd-1\expndtw-4  \expnd0\expndtw0 a\expnd-1\expndtw-4  \expnd0\expndtw0 list of saved cams in the Test Library. Some cams are examples provided by Performance Trends.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 As you run\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 cams yourself and save the results,\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 you will add many more cams to the library.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 These saved files are useful for making comparisons in the future, and can be used as cam patterns (or templates) for new cams (saving you considerable time by not having to type in specs which match a past\f0\fs20\expnd16\expndtw80\charscalex100  \expnd-1\expndtw-4 cam).\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li806\ri7416\sl244\slmult1\sb223\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 Figure 2.2 shows that the Test Library is divided into sections (called Folders in Figure 2.2)\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 to help organize a large number of cams.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 For example, all cams for the company ABC Engines could be saved under a section name of ABC-ENG.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 All\expnd-1\expndtw-4  \expnd0\expndtw0 4\expnd-1\expndtw-4  \expnd0\expndtw0 cylinder\expnd-1\expndtw-4  \expnd0\expndtw0 Ford\expnd-1\expndtw-4  \expnd0\expndtw0 cams\expnd-1\expndtw-4  \expnd0\expndtw0 could\expnd-1\expndtw-4  \expnd0\expndtw0 be saved under a section name of 4CYL-FORD.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 This\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 will\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 save\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 considerable\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 time and confusion when trying to located a particular cam in the future.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 To look in different sections, click on the Folder name from the list shown at the lower right\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 of Figure 2.2.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 The list of cams will then be updated for that Folder.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 To pick a cam, simply click on it from the list of cams, then click on the Open button.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 (For those familiar with computers, Folders are actually subdirectories or folders in the CAMDATA folder.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 The Name \'93Folder\'94 can be changed to something else, like \'93Customer\'94 in the Preferences menu.)\par\sect\sectd\sbkpage\headery725\footery725\margtsxn1100\margbsxn920
