\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li969\ri4095\sl244\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 Most all of the Cam Analyzer's features allow you to compare one cam to another.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 For\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 example,\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 you\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 can\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 print\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 a\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 Duration\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 Report\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 for\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 2\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 cams\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 and\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 compare the results.\expnd16\expndtw80  \expnd0\expndtw0 Click on Report at the top of the Main Screen for the Report Menu of Figure 4.21 and select Duration Report as the Type.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 Figure 4.22 shows 2 Duration reports, one for the UD6060S.R07, and another for the XDRAG.PTI \expnd-1\expndtw-4 cam.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb9\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li969\ri4239\qj\sl244\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 Another useful feature is to compare 2 or more cams graphically on the Graph screen.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 For\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 example,\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 let's\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 compare\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 the\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 intake\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 lobe\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 of\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 the\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 UD6060S.R07\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 to\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 the XDRAG.PTI\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 (same as CC8094S.R04) cam from Example 4.1.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb2\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li969\ri4095\sl244\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 Click on Graph at the top of the Main Screen and select Intake Cam Data as the Graph Type.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 See Figure 4.23.\expnd16\expndtw80  \expnd0\expndtw0 Set only Graph Lift to Yes so you will only graph\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 Cam\expnd-1\expndtw-4  \expnd0\expndtw0 Lift.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 Set\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 Lift\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 Filtering\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 to\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 Some\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 (since\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 this\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 profile\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 was\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 also\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 measured by hand) and Vel/Accel/Jerk Filtering to None.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 Then click on Make Graph to produce the graph of Figure 4.24.\par\sect\sectd\sbkpage\headery725\footery743\margtsxn1100\margbsxn940
