ements we used to do.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 We recommend setting this to Yes.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 No should only be used if you want to repeat results from an older version of Cam Analyzer.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb12\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s6\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li806\sl240\slmult1\f2\fs36\b1\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 A4.4\expnd7\expndtw34\charscalex150  \expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 Troubleshooting\expnd-1\expndtw-7  \expnd0\expndtw0 Communications\expnd-1\expndtw-7  \expnd0\expndtw0 to\expnd-1\expndtw-7  \expnd0\expndtw-2 Electronics\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li806\ri391\sl244\slmult1\sb236\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 If you find that the program can not communicate with the Black Box, you may first want to let the program try to \'93Find\'94 it as shown in Figure A4.4.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 If it can not be found, check the Troubleshooting features built into the Cam Analyzer in Figure A4.17. The first test available of \'93Test Com Port\'94 is a very easy test to pass.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 That means if you can not pass it, there is a definite problem with the computer\'92s Com port, or the cable, or you are doing the test wrong.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 If the problem proves to be with the computer (which is usually does), then you must contact your computer repair shop.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 You could also switch to a USB to Com port\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 converter if you have a USB\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 port.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 (USB-Com\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 port\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 converters are typically\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 not\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 as reliable as a true Com\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 port.)\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 The \'93Check Boot Message\'94 is a more thorough test, and checks both the Com port and cable, and some basic functioning of the Black Box.\par\sect\sectd\sbkpage\headery725\footery743\margtsxn1100\margbsxn940
